  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A dense oxide coating such as Al2O3 or ZrO2 can be deposited by CVD or PVD on a boride-based component.",
      "field": "hypothesis; intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9959495::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Applying the oxide coating will significantly reduce molten-aluminum corrosion at 700–750 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9959495::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The deposited oxide film will be dense and adherent.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9959495::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer will impede direct contact between molten aluminum and the boride substrate.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer will suppress dissolution of the underlying boride matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The chemically stable oxide film will lower interdiffusion between molten aluminum and the substrate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower interdiffusion and prevention of reactive attack will reduce substrate wear and mass loss.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boride-containing surfaces can provide corrosion and wear resistance relevant to equipment used in aluminum casting environments.",
      "field": "material_initial_state; supporting evidence rationale",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10221107::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continuous or batch molten-aluminum exposure at 700–750 °C is typical of hot-dip aluminum-plating lines.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating is expected to remain effective during molten-aluminum immersion under limited-oxygen or inert conditions.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 100 hours, the coated substrate will show 30–50% lower mass loss than an equivalent uncoated boride substrate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 100 hours, the coated substrate will have fewer intermetallic reaction layers than the uncoated control.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Protection depends on the coating remaining free of cracks and delamination.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
